                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002082"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0040016"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002087"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000106"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The first few specialized divisions of an activated animal egg; Stage consisting of division of cells in the early embryo. The zygotes of many species undergo rapid cell cycles with no significant growth, producing a cluster of cells the same size as the original zygote. The different cells derived from cleavage are called blastomeres and form a compact mass called the morula. Cleavage ends with the formation of the blastula.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BILS:0000107</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BilaDO:0000006</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
