        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Small indentation on the inferior surface of the cerebral cortex at the border of the occiptal and parietal lobes. It is considered as a landmark because the occipital lobe is located just behind the line that connects that notch with the parietoccipital sulcus (adapted from Wikipedia).</obo:IAO_0000115>
