    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002752 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002752">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0007702"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0014649"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The olivocerebellar tract (olivocerebellar fibers) leaves the olivary nucleus and pass out through the hilum and decussate with those from the opposite olive in the raphé, then as internal arcuate fibers they pass partly through and partly around the opposite olive and enter the inferior peduncle to be distributed to the cerebellar hemisphere of the opposite side from which they arise. They terminate directly on Purkinje cells as the climbing fiber input system. [WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:oc</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:oct</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BIRNLEX:1579</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DHBA:12747</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:72638</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MBA:404</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Olivocerebellar_tract</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>olivocerebellar tract</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>olivocerebellar tract</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002752"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The olivocerebellar tract (olivocerebellar fibers) leaves the olivary nucleus and pass out through the hilum and decussate with those from the opposite olive in the raphé, then as internal arcuate fibers they pass partly through and partly around the opposite olive and enter the inferior peduncle to be distributed to the cerebellar hemisphere of the opposite side from which they arise. They terminate directly on Purkinje cells as the climbing fiber input system. [WP,unvetted].</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Olivocerebellar_tract</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002753 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002753">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001018"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005413"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002216"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0019230"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>It ascends the dorsal part of the lateral funiculus and enters the cerebellum via the restiform body. Within the cerebellum, its axons terminate in the ipsilateral hindlimb area of the anterior lobe and in the pyramis and the paramedian lobule predominantly ipsilaterally. Rostrally, it extends to lobules I and II. Afferents from the upper trunk, forelimbs, and the neck to the cerebellum.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:dsc</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:psc</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:sctd</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BIRNLEX:1585</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BM:DSCT</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DHBA:12746</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DMBA:17761</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:72641</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MBA:553</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:369284002</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Dorsal_spinocerebellar_tract</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>dorsal spinocerebellar tract</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>flechsig&apos;s tract</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>posterior spinocerebellar tract</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>posterior spinocerebellar tract</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002753"/>
