            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The dorsal trigeminal tract (dorsal trigeminothalamic tract, or lemniscus) is a tract which receives signals from Meissner&apos;s corpuscles and Pacinian corpuscles. this tract arises from Principal trigeminal nucleus and terminates in the VPM nucleus of the thalamus. [WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:d5</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:tth</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BIRNLEX:1718</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DHBA:12736</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:72500</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
