            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Nucleus in the pontine tegmentum of most mammals that receives projections from the ventral cochlear nucleus via the large specialized synapse, the Calyx of Held. It is not clear whether a well defined nucleus is present in humans, although humans may possess scattered cells with similar input.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BIRNLEX:2595</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DHBA:12460</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:75732</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>medial nucleus of trapezoid body</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>medial nucleus of trapezoid body</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
