    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002972 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002972">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0015233"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002733"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>In the anatomy of the brain, the centromedian nucleus, also known as the centrum medianum, (CM or Cm-Pf) is a part of the intralaminar nucleus (ILN) of the thalamus. There are two centromedian nuclei arranged bilaterally. It contains about 2000 neurons per cubic millimetre and has a volume of about 310 cubic millimetres with 664,000 neurons in total. [WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:CM</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:CMn</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
