    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003004 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003004">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0007415"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004684"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The median raphe nucleus (or superior central nucleus) is composed of polygonal, fusiform and pyriform neurons and exists rostral to the nucleus raphe pontis. One trait of the MRN is its inhibition by lysergic acid diethylamide and psilocin, two serotonin antagonist hallucinogens. The inactivation of the nucleus centralis superior via LSD produces a dose dependent inactivation in the MRN, but not in the raphe pallidus[WP,unvetted].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BAMS:MnR</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BIRNLEX:889</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BM:MR</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DHBA:12235</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:35551</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:72465</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MBA:679</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Median_raphe_nucleus</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>neuronames:1391</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>MRN</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>cell group b8</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>medial raphe nucleus</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>median nucleus of the raphe</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>superior central nucleus</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>superior central nucleus raphe</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>superior central tegmental nucleus</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>median raphe nucleus</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>median raphe nucleus</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003004"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The median raphe nucleus (or superior central nucleus) is composed of polygonal, fusiform and pyriform neurons and exists rostral to the nucleus raphe pontis. One trait of the MRN is its inhibition by lysergic acid diethylamide and psilocin, two serotonin antagonist hallucinogens. The inactivation of the nucleus centralis superior via LSD produces a dose dependent inactivation in the MRN, but not in the raphe pallidus[WP,unvetted].</owl:annotatedTarget>
