    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0006695 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0006695">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0011215"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002206"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The mammillary axonal complex is formed by the axons from the lateral, medial mammillary and the dorsal premammillary nuclei which share a branching pattern. Every neuron gives off one axonal stem that bifurcates into 2 branches. One of the branches is directed dorsally to the thalamus and another caudally to the midbrain[GO].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>mammillary axonal complex</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>mammillary axonal complex</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0006695"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The mammillary axonal complex is formed by the axons from the lateral, medial mammillary and the dorsal premammillary nuclei which share a branching pattern. Every neuron gives off one axonal stem that bifurcates into 2 branches. One of the branches is directed dorsally to the thalamus and another caudally to the midbrain[GO].</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0061373</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


