        <obo:IAO_0000115>The hemorrhoidal plexus (or rectal venous plexus) surrounds the rectum, and communicates in front with the vesical venous plexus in the male, and the uterovaginal plexus in the female. A free communication between the portal and systemic venous systems is established through the hemorrhoidal plexus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:18933</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C32728</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
