            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A duct that is located within a lobule, with no more connective tissue intervening between ducts and secretory units (i.e., acini or tubules) than between adjacent secretory units. Intercalated and striated ducts are intralobular.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:205214009</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>intralobular duct</rdfs:label>
