        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0034734"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The medial olfactory stria turns medialward behind the parolfactory area and ends in the subcallosal gyrus; in some cases a small intermediate stria is seen running backward to the anterior perforated substance.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Medial_olfactory_stria</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0034743 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0034743">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0022248"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0011299"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0022247"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The inferior longitudinal fasciculus connects the temporal lobe and occipital lobe, running along the lateral walls of the inferior and posterior cornua of the lateral ventricle. The existence of this fasciculus independent from the occipitotemporal fasciculus has been questioned for the human being, such that it has been proposed that the term inferior longitudinal fasciculus be replaced by the term &apos;occipitotemporal projection&apos;.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DHBA:10580</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:77632</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>HBA:9260</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NeuroNamesCNID:538</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:369085008</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Inferior_longitudinal_fasciculus</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>neuronames:1443</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:label>inferior longitudinal fasciculus</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel>inferior longitudinal fasciculus</skos:prefLabel>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0034743"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The inferior longitudinal fasciculus connects the temporal lobe and occipital lobe, running along the lateral walls of the inferior and posterior cornua of the lateral ventricle. The existence of this fasciculus independent from the occipitotemporal fasciculus has been questioned for the human being, such that it has been proposed that the term inferior longitudinal fasciculus be replaced by the term &apos;occipitotemporal projection&apos;.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Inferior_longitudinal_fasciculus</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


